@startuml KAIA Wallet Cryptographic Authentication Flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam maxmessagesize 60

title KAIA Wallet Cryptographic Authentication Flow\nChallenge-Response Protocol with ECDSA Signature Verification

actor User as U
participant "Frontend\n(WalletModal)" as FE
participant "KAIA Wallet\n(Kaikas)" as WALLET
participant "Backend\n(Controller)" as BE
participant "KAIA Auth\nService" as SVC
participant "Challenge Store\n(In-Memory)" as STORE

== Challenge Generation Phase ==
U -> FE: Click "Connect with KAIA Wallet"
activate FE

FE -> WALLET: Check wallet availability\nwindow.klaytn exists?
activate WALLET
WALLET -> FE: Wallet available
deactivate WALLET

FE -> BE: GET /auth/kaia/challenge
activate BE

BE -> SVC: generateChallenge()
activate SVC

SVC -> SVC: Generate cryptographically secure nonce\nrandomBytes(32).toString('hex')
SVC -> SVC: Create timestamp\nMath.floor(Date.now() / 1000)
SVC -> SVC: Generate challenge ID\nrandomBytes(16).toString('hex')

SVC -> SVC: Construct challenge message:\n"Sign in to MultiWallet\\n" +\n"Domain: line.depick.wtf\\n" +\n"Nonce: 0x1234567890abcdef...\\n" +\n"Timestamp: 1673123456"

SVC -> STORE: Store challenge\n{ challengeId, nonce, timestamp, domain, expiresAt }
activate STORE
STORE -> SVC: Challenge stored (5 min expiry)
deactivate STORE

SVC -> BE: { challengeId, message, expiresAt }
deactivate SVC

BE -> FE: HTTP 200:\n{ challengeId, message, expiresAt }
deactivate BE

== Wallet Connection & Signature Phase ==
FE -> WALLET: window.klaytn.enable()\nRequest wallet connection
activate WALLET

WALLET -> U: Show connection prompt\n"Connect to MultiWallet?"
U -> WALLET: Approve connection

WALLET -> FE: Return wallet address\naccounts[0] = "0x742C...4BaB"
deactivate WALLET

FE -> FE: Store wallet address\nconst address = accounts[0]

FE -> WALLET: window.klaytn.sign(message, address)\nRequest signature for challenge
activate WALLET

note over WALLET: ECDSA Signature Generation:\n1. Hash message with Keccak-256\n2. Sign hash with private key (secp256k1)\n3. Return signature components (r, s, v)

WALLET -> U: Show signature prompt\n"Sign message for authentication?"
U -> WALLET: Approve signature

WALLET -> WALLET: **CRYPTOGRAPHIC OPERATION**:\nPrivate key signs message hash\n(Private key NEVER leaves wallet)

WALLET -> FE: Return ECDSA signature\n"0x1234567890abcdef..." (r, s, v)
deactivate WALLET

== Signature Verification Phase ==
FE -> BE: POST /auth/kaia/verify\nContent-Type: application/json\n{ challengeId, address, signature, message }
activate BE

BE -> SVC: verifySignature(challengeId, address, signature, message)
activate SVC

SVC -> STORE: Retrieve challenge\nchallenge = store.get(challengeId)
activate STORE
STORE -> SVC: Return challenge data
deactivate STORE

SVC -> SVC: **CHALLENGE VALIDATION**:\n1. Verify challenge exists\n2. Check not expired (< 5 minutes)\n3. Mark challenge as consumed

SVC -> STORE: Delete used challenge\nstore.delete(challengeId)
activate STORE
STORE -> SVC: Challenge consumed
deactivate STORE

SVC -> SVC: **MESSAGE VERIFICATION**:\nReconstruct expected message:\n"Sign in to MultiWallet\\n" +\n"Domain: line.depick.wtf\\n" +\n"Nonce: stored_nonce\\n" +\n"Timestamp: stored_timestamp"

SVC -> SVC: **CRYPTOGRAPHIC VERIFICATION**:\n1. Hash message with Keccak-256\n2. Recover public key from signature\n   ecrecover(hash, v, r, s)\n3. Derive address from public key\n   keccak256(publicKey).slice(-20)\n4. Compare derived vs claimed address

alt Signature Verification Successful
    SVC -> SVC: **JWT TOKEN CREATION**:\nCreate payload:\n{ provider: 'kaia',\n  address: verifiedAddress,\n  chainId: 8217,\n  verified: true,\n  authenticatedAt: timestamp }\nSign with JWT_SECRET (1h expiry)
    
    SVC -> BE: { jwtToken, userData }
    deactivate SVC
    
    BE -> FE: HTTP 200:\n{ success: true,\n  auth_token: JWT_TOKEN,\n  user_data: { address, chainId, verified } }
    deactivate BE
    
    FE -> FE: Create user session:\n{ provider: 'kaia',\n  address: userData.address,\n  chainId: userData.chainId,\n  verified: userData.verified,\n  token: auth_token }
    
    FE -> FE: onAuthSuccess(userData)\nStore JWT token in session
    
    FE -> U: Show "Connected" status\nDisplay: "Connected: kaia (0x742C...4BaB)"
    deactivate FE

else Verification Failed
    SVC -> BE: throw Error("Signature verification failed")
    deactivate SVC
    
    BE -> FE: HTTP 400: Verification failed
    deactivate BE
    
    FE -> U: Show error message
    deactivate FE
end

== Security Properties Achieved ==
note over U, STORE: **Cryptographic Security Guarantees:**\n• Private key never transmitted or exposed\n• Mathematical proof of wallet ownership\n• Single-use challenge prevents replay attacks\n• Domain binding prevents cross-site reuse\n• Time-bound authentication (5 minute window)\n• ECDSA signature provides non-repudiation

== Alternative Error Flows ==
note over SVC, BE: **Error Scenarios:**\n• Wallet not available → User prompted to install Kaikas\n• User rejects connection → Connection canceled\n• User rejects signature → Authentication failed\n• Challenge expired → Request new challenge\n• Invalid signature → Cryptographic verification failed\n• Network error → Retry mechanism

@enduml